Decision 37 with log-2026-09-24 "Revised", clean: a construct Kind applies in a generated mode
only, so a variant-level export fn (TYPES.md §12.1, DECISIONS 226) draws no VariantMethod under a
go emit in types mode, which no generator writes yet; the day one is generated, its rules take
VariantMethod and this case fails. A ts emit, generated, reports it: findings/E8019_61.txtar.
-- a/a.canon --
package a

/// A reward.
variant Reward {
  /// Some gold.
  gold {
    /// How much.
    amount: Int
  }
  /// Nothing.
  nothing

  /// What it is worth.
  export fn worth(self) -> Int {
    return match self {
      gold(g) => g.amount
      nothing => 0
    }
  }

  check worth() >= 0 else "negative"
}

emit go { out: "@features/a", package: "a", mode: types }
-- findings.txt --
0 errors, 0 warnings in 1 package (…)
